<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Arthur MacArthur Jr.</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1845">1845</a>–<a href="/years/1912">1912</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Arthur MacArthur Jr. was an American general who served as military governor of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philippines">Philippines</a> in 1900 and 1901, during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philippine-american-war">Philippine–American War</a>. His forces captured <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emilio-aguinaldo">Emilio Aguinaldo</a> in March 1901, and he handed over civil authority to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-howard-taft">William Howard Taft</a>. He was the father of General <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/douglas-macarthur">Douglas MacArthur</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/arthur-macarthur-jr.jpg" alt="Arthur MacArthur Jr." width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Arthur_MacArthur_while_serving_as_governor_of_the_Philippines_Trim.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
